WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:14.402
Vinnie and Mandy froze with fear.

2
00:00:14.403 --> 00:00:18.538
All the sailors stopped rowing or woke up.

3
00:00:18.539 --> 00:00:21.141
They stared at the children.

4
00:00:21.142 --> 00:00:25.340
The large man walked over to Vinnie and Mandy.

5
00:00:25.341 --> 00:00:29.142
Mandy guessed he was the captain.

6
00:00:29.143 --> 00:00:35.959
“Gunnar! Explain! Who are they?” the captain asked the fair boy.

7
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:39.867
“Sir, I don’t know,” the boy replied.

8
00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:42.008
“Why did you hide here?

9
00:00:42.009 --> 00:00:45.012
Do you want to be warriors like Gunnar?”

10
00:00:45.013 --> 00:00:49.916
The captain pointed his sword at Vinnie and Mandy.

11
00:00:49.917 --> 00:00:52.612
“Yes, sir!” Vinnie shouted.

12
00:00:52.613 --> 00:00:57.400
“Ah, true Viking spirit!” the captain said.

13
00:00:57.401 --> 00:01:00.282
“I like your courage, boy.”

14
00:01:00.283 --> 00:01:04.001
The captain slapped Vinnie on the back.

15
00:01:04.002 --> 00:01:07.404
Vinnie nearly fell over.

16
00:01:07.405 --> 00:01:11.016
The captain stopped and glared at Mandy.

17
00:01:11.017 --> 00:01:16.134
“But you! Little girls should not be sneaking onto a Viking ship.

18
00:01:16.135 --> 00:01:20.013
Especially one as weak as you,” he sneered.

19
00:01:20.014 --> 00:01:23.606
Mandy threw back her head proudly.

20
00:01:23.607 --> 00:01:29.481
“I may look weak, sir,” she replied in a clear, loud voice.

21
00:01:29.482 --> 00:01:32.586
“But I am as strong as a horse.”

22
00:01:32.587 --> 00:01:36.876
“Land ho!” the lookout shouted.

23
00:01:36.877 --> 00:01:39.679
“Finally!” the captain said.

24
00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.136
“Get ready to go ashore.”

25
00:01:42.137 --> 00:01:45.414
Turning to Vinnie and Mandy, he said,

26
00:01:45.415 --> 00:01:49.400
“You two—stay with Gunnar.”

27
00:01:49.401 --> 00:01:54.695
Mandy let out a sigh of relief as the captain turned away.

28
00:01:54.696 --> 00:02:00.535
“Vinnie! I don’t think he likes me being on the ship,” she said.

29
00:02:00.536 --> 00:02:05.421
“Don’t worry. You were really brave,” Vinnie replied.

30
00:02:05.422 --> 00:02:07.601
He turned to Gunnar.

31
00:02:07.602 --> 00:02:11.163
“Where are we going?” he asked.

32
00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:13.735
“This port is Kaupang.

33
00:02:13.736 --> 00:02:20.145
It is a Viking village where we trade and sell our goods,” Gunnar said proudly.

34
00:02:20.146 --> 00:02:23.227
“The captain is the best bear hunter!

35
00:02:23.228 --> 00:02:27.402
He brought bear skins from our village in the icy North.”

36
00:02:27.403 --> 00:02:30.600
“Here we go, Vinnie. Look!”

37
00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:34.217
Mandy grabbed his arm.

38
00:02:34.218 --> 00:02:38.616
The Sleeping Dragon pulled smoothly into port.

39
00:02:38.617 --> 00:02:43.327
Several other Viking ships were already docked there.

40
00:02:43.328 --> 00:02:46.419
Each ship was long and slender.

41
00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:51.405
Viking sailors carried large chests out of the ships.

42
00:02:51.406 --> 00:02:56.143
Some carried smaller boxes of jewelry.

43
00:02:56.144 --> 00:02:59.470
“Gunnar!” the captain called out.

44
00:02:59.471 --> 00:03:03.410
“Take this to Old Dirk, the blacksmith.”

45
00:03:03.411 --> 00:03:07.904
The captain handed Gunnar a jewelry box.

46
00:03:07.905 --> 00:03:10.082
“Tell him I sent you.

47
00:03:10.083 --> 00:03:12.473
He will know what to do.”

48
00:03:12.474 --> 00:03:17.075
“Yes, captain,” said Gunnar as he took the box.

49
00:03:17.076 --> 00:03:21.415
“Do not disappoint me,” the captain roared.

50
00:03:21.416 --> 00:03:24.383
“And keep an eye on those two.”

51
00:03:24.384 --> 00:03:26.896
He pointed to Vinnie and Mandy.

52
00:03:26.897 --> 00:03:29.953
“Come on!” Gunnar called.

53
00:03:29.954 --> 00:03:34.804
Vinnie and Mandy followed him off the Sleeping Dragon.

54
00:03:34.805 --> 00:03:38.607
Kaupang was a busy open market.

55
00:03:38.608 --> 00:03:42.800
People exchanged furs for iron weapons.

56
00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:49.733
Others bought bear skins, walrus tusks, and whale bones with silver coins.

57
00:03:49.734 --> 00:03:55.000
Finally the children arrived at the blacksmith’s workshop.

58
00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:58.871
The boy introduced himself to the blacksmith.

59
00:03:58.872 --> 00:04:03.411
“I am Gunnar. Captain Skull-Crusher sent me.”

60
00:04:03.412 --> 00:04:06.612
Vinnie and Mandy stared at each other.

61
00:04:06.613 --> 00:04:13.767
“Skull-Crusher?” they gasped.
